---
/**
 * The load-bearing clauses here are the non-medical scope note and the
 * emergency instruction. Both restate what the site says elsewhere in its own
 * copy, which is the point: the terms should not be the first place a reader
 * learns Quantum does not do skilled nursing.
 *
 * The site is a brochure with contact forms — no accounts, no payments, no
 * user content — so there is nothing here about billing or account security.
 * Add those if that ever changes.
 *
 * NOT REVIEWED BY COUNSEL. The limitation-of-liability and governing-law
 * sections in particular are boilerplate that a lawyer should confirm.
 */

// COMPONENTS
import LegalPage from "@/components/LegalPage.astro";

// DATA
import { baseData, telHref, mailHref } from "@/data/siteData";
---

<LegalPage
  title="Terms & Conditions"
  updated="September 8, 2026"
  pageTitle={`Terms & Conditions | ${baseData.title}`}
  description="The terms that apply when you use the Quantum Home Cares website."
>
  <p class="lead">
    These terms apply to your use of this website. By browsing the site or sending us a form, you
    agree to them. If you do not, please do not use the site.
  </p>

  <h2>What this website is</h2>

  <p>
    This site describes the services {baseData.legalName} offers and gives you a way to reach us. It is
    information, not an offer of care and not a contract to provide it.
  </p>

  <h2>No care relationship until we agree to one</h2>

  <p>
    Sending a form does not make you a client. We take care relationships on only after we have
    spoken with you, assessed the situation, confirmed we can staff it, and put a written service
    agreement in place. That agreement, not this website, governs the care we provide.
  </p>

  <h2>We are a non-medical provider</h2>

  <div class="legal-callout">
    <p>
      <strong>Nothing on this site is medical advice.</strong> We provide non-medical home care. We do
      not deliver skilled nursing services such as wound care, injections, or IV therapy, and nothing
      here should be used to decide about anyone's treatment. Talk to a physician or a licensed clinician
      about medical questions.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>In an emergency, call 911.</strong> This website is not monitored around the clock, and
      a form submission is not a way to get urgent help.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Using the site</h2>

  <p>You agree not to:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>Submit false information, or someone else's information without the right to share it.</li>
    <li>Use the forms to send unsolicited advertising.</li>
    <li>Attempt to disrupt, overload, or gain unauthorized access to the site.</li>
    <li>Copy the site's content for a competing commercial purpose.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Information you send us</h2>

  <p>
    When you send us details about another person, whether as a family member or as a referring
    professional, you confirm you are entitled to share them. What we do with what you send is
    covered in our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Our content</h2>

  <p>
    The text, photographs, and design on this site belong to {baseData.legalName} or are used with permission.
    You may read and share pages, but please do not republish the content as your own.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>

  <p>
    Some pages link to outside organizations, including the resources we gather for families. We
    offer those links to be useful. We do not control those sites, we are not responsible for what
    they say, and a link is not an endorsement. Programs and eligibility rules change, so confirm
    anything important directly with the organization that runs it.
  </p>

  <h2>Accuracy</h2>

  <p>
    We work to keep this site accurate and current, but we do not guarantee that every detail is
    complete or up to date. Service availability, response times, and coverage can change.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>

  <p>
    To the extent the law allows, {baseData.legalName} is not liable for indirect or consequential losses
    arising from your use of this website. Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot lawfully
    be limited, and nothing here affects the terms of a signed service agreement between us.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>

  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of the State of New Jersey, and disputes about them belong
    in the courts of New Jersey.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>

  <p>
    We may update these terms. The current version always lives on this page, with the date it
    changed at the top.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact us</h2>

  <p>
    Questions about these terms can go to <a href={mailHref}>{baseData.email}</a> or <a
      href={telHref}>{baseData.phone}</a
    >.
  </p>

  <p>{baseData.legalName} · {baseData.credentials.license}</p>
</LegalPage>
